+
+## Follow-up cloud browser review and encoding fix
+Parent's supported cloud browser observed all eight fixture responses, the photo, and an actual JSON export with current custom values/provenance/zero real fits. It found mojibake only on the narrow-layout QA page: the HTML lacked a charset declaration. Both copies now declare UTF-8 at the start of the head and use ASCII HTML entities for the middle dot and multiplication signs. A byte/structure regression covers the declaration, labels, absence of corrupted text and candidate/shipped equality. Rendered recheck of this correction remains with the parent browser reviewer. Scientific code is unchanged.
+
+The parent cloud browser also passed 390/768-width iframe layouts, fold shifts/reset and all eight fixtures. Displayed machine status `ok` is now phrased “residual computed,” so a valid calculation cannot be mistaken for scientific fit acceptance. The exported machine status is unchanged.
